{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1547250-example-naval-combat","id":1547250,"title":"Example naval combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-26T05:19:39-08:00","id":1547250,"title":"Example naval combat","content":"I did an example of ship combat. I'd love some critiques and thoughts on system.<br /> <br /> Pakpow (Exegent of the puppet god) has recently become aware of a realm scion who wishes to avoid his arranged marriage and elope with his lover. She has happily taken a fortune of his money to see him smuggled out of her city of Zhaoj\u016bn, simultaneously weakening the power of political rivals while enriching herself.<br /> <br /> She chooses the night of a storm to take her ship lair out of the docks and transport her client out of town. Only one of the chosen has the skill to navigate in this weather, and, amid the rain and fog, hiding her own identity is less challenging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-26T05:20:14-08:00","id":1547251,"title":"","content":"Peleps Dejan has the responsibility to see that her young, unexalted, kinsman does not elope and thereby screw up the delicate negotiations that went into his marriage. She also has money and connections, and those have, in turn, provided her a competent collection of informants and spies who are able to communicate the movements of this love-struck youth the moment he begins his insufficiently secret trip to the docks.<br /> <br /> Dejan quickly moves her (ready and waiting, because money gets you things) ship out of its moorings. On a stormy night like tonight only a reckless youth, a person who has taken leave of their senses, or an exalted would be out on the water. She expects no difficulty in finding and retrieving her young relative.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-26T05:20:59-08:00","id":1547252,"title":"","content":"The conflict begins in a maze of docks within a protective breakwater. It is dark, there is a significant storm going on; vision is difficult, rain is pouring out of the sky, winds and waves batter the ships. Rolls involving vison will take a two-die penalty, most sailing rolls will have a difficulty of 3 inside the breakwater and difficulty 4 outside of it (it may make more sense to sometimes give the ships a penalty instead, I\u2019ll see).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-26T05:22:09-08:00","id":1547253,"title":"","content":"Pakpow is piloting a large yacht, her lair, with the aid of animated puppets. The Peleps scion has been ushered into the hold and hidden there. He doesn\u2019t realize that he has been locked in, he is unaware that the ship is being sailed by automatons.<br /> <br /> Pakpow has 4 dots in sail with a specialty of her lair and 4 dots of wits. She is using Ship self-puppetry and Silken sail meditation. She has 7 motes committed (To Ship-Self puppetry and Spider in her Webs) and has used 1 willpower . Her mote pools start at 12/12 personal and 20/27 peripheral. She has 6/7 willpower available.<br /> <br /> Her Yacht/lair has the following characteristics Speed Current +1, Sail +2, Charms +2 Maneuverability 0, Hull -1/-2/-4/incapacitated Crew no penalty for puppets.<br /> <br /> Dejan is Piloting an Imperial trireme with a crew of marines aboard. She has three dots of wits and five dots of sail with a specialty in war gallies. She has 13/13 personal and 31/31 peripheral. She has 5/5 willpower,<br /> <br /> Her warship has these characteristics Speed Current +1, Sail +2, Oars +2 Maneuverability +2, Hull -1/-2/-4/incapacitated, Crew no modifier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-26T05:23:56-08:00","id":1547254,"title":"","content":"With the darkness, rain, fog, wind and rough seas the ships can barely see one another. The ships are close enough to one another to engage in combat without doing a pursuit test (core p244)<br /> <br /> Neither ship has enough momentum to do what they wish (escape in the case of Pakpow and a boarding action for Peleps Dejan). So, on round 1 both ships perform positioning actions.<br /> <br /> Pakpow\u2019s puppets on the deck put other puppets on the end of long poles. These puppets grasp the sea floor, docks, and other ships giving Pokpow\u2019s craft something solid to push and pull against. Pokpow can\u2019t win a fight against that many marines, especially when lead by an exalted captain. She goes all in, she has a pool of 9 dice uses a full excellency of 5 dice She gets a two-point stunt for an additional two dice and a success, furthermore she uses a willpower for an additional success. With a good roll she gets 14 successes (12 on her 16 dice and two additional).<br /> <br /> Dejan confidently shouts orders to her crew, her voice cutting through the storm. She feels the sway of the water in her elemental soul twisting the rudder with a supernatural precision granted by her water aspected exaltation. Her pool is 9 dice, she uses her full excellency of three bonus successes from Fine Passage negotiating style and receives two dice for her stunt, she gets another two dice for the maneuverability of the trireme. Her dice only turn up three successes, plus an additional success on a re-rolled 6 (from fine passage negotiating style) for a total of 7.<br /> <br /> Pakpow has 14 successes this gives her 16 momentum (+2 because it is the first time she has used the positioning action this scene).<br /> <br /> Dejon gains four momentum, because a positioning strategy always grants momentum equal to the ship\u2019s maneuverability even when the ship loses the opposed roll and because this is the first time she has used the positioning action this scene and she gets an additional 2 from her positioning test (Crucible of Legend p73).<br /> <br /> Pakpow is at 7/12 personal and 20/27 peripheral. She still has 6/7 willpower available (she spent one but gained one from her stunt).<br /> Dejan is at 7/13 personal and 31/31 peripheral. She has 5/5 willpower, she is in water aura.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-26T05:26:15-08:00","id":1547255,"title":"","content":"Round 2<br /> <br /> Pakpow uses her Puppets on poles to pull her ship into position to catch the wind in her sails. She'll do this by grasping on to other ships, one of which has come loose in the storm. This enables her to push it in the direction of Dejon\u2019s warship. Pakpow will spend 10 momentum (discounted 2 because it is the first time in the scene that she is trying this) to try and escape. She will again spend willpower. Her dice pool is 9 with 5 bonus dice from her excellency, 2 from her stunt and 4 from her vessel\u2019s speed. She gets two automatic successes one from her willpower and one from her stunt. She gets 11 successes all together.<br /> <br /> Dejan was surprised by the unnatural movement of the yacht, she realizes that whatever is piloting the other vessel is more than human. She uses her mastery of water to nudge the waves in a fashion to speed her passage. She again uses a full excellency and supplements it with Ocean Darting Maneuver (What Fire Has Wrought page 257) she also supplements the roll with a willpower and is also granted a two-point stunt. She rolls 13 (pool + stunt, +maneuver score) dice with double 9\u2019s and rerolling 6\u2019s and adds 6 automatic successes- 12 successes not as bad as last time but not great either.<br /> <br /> Dejan won the test by 1 success, however the text from Crucible of Legend is \u201ca successful roll grants momentum equal to its successes\u201d not net successes, successes full stop. Dejan gains 12 momentum.<br /> <br /> Pakpow is at 7/12 personal and 20/27 peripheral. She still has 6/7 willpower. Her ship has 6 momentum.<br /> Dejan is at 1/13 personal and 31/31 peripheral. She has 5/5 willpower, she is in water aura. Her ship has 16 momentum.<br /> Both exalted recover 5 motes\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-26T05:27:36-08:00","id":1547256,"title":"","content":"Round 3<br /> <br /> Both Exalted recover 5 motes of essence.<br /> <br /> Pakpow clears the breakwater, she takes her faster, lighter, but less maneuverable ship on a path along the outside of the rocky breakwater racing the waves in hopes that she can squeeze in front of the ones that will smash her pursuer. She tries positioning again and, being in dire circumstances, continues to use a full excellency augmented by spending a willpower. She rolls 9 from her pool, 5 from her excellency, and 2 from the stunt (only a level 1 stunt this round). With the willpower she achieves 6 successes.<br /> <br /> Exhorting oarsmen to give her their all, Dejan points her bow straight at the oncoming waves to slice through them then spins her ship about to ride the waves straight at Pakpow\u2019s yacht. She spends 6 momentum (discounted by 2) to try a boarding maneuver augmented with a Full excellency from Fine Passage Negotiating Style, Ocean Darting Maneuver, and a willpower. She rolls 9 from her pool, 2 from her maneuverability, 2 from her stunt (a level 2), she adds 5 automatic successes, (from fine passage negotiating style, her stunt and her willpower) she doubles nines, and she rerolls sixes. A great roll -17 successes.<br /> <br /> Pakpow gains 1 momentum<br /> <br /> Pakpow is at 7/12 personal and 20/27 peripheral. She still has 5/7 willpower. Her ship has 7 momentum<br /> Dejan is at 0/13 personal and 26/31 peripheral. She has 5/5 willpower, she is in water aura, her anima is at glowing. Her ship has 10 momentum.<br /> <br /> <b>Because the boarding action was successful, the naval combat ends</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 01-21-2025, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-26T05:28:16-08:00","id":1547257,"title":"","content":"Pakpow knows that she can not face that many marines. she jumps into a large submersible puppet with a diving bell contraption in it and sneakily has it walk back to Zhaoj\u016bn along the sea floor. She distracts attention from herself by scuttling her ship, perhaps the Peleps boy will die, that would still serve her purposes. On the way back she roughs out her demands for compensation from house Peleps whose young Scion stole her Yacht and somehow managed to sink it.<br /> <br /> Dejan with her ability to function under water manages to save her crew and her young kinsman but in the effort to do so, the opposing Captain escapes. Dejan does take the time collect several puppets to investigate who was working against her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-26T05:32:24-08:00","id":1547258,"title":"","content":"My takeaway is the alterations made in Crucible of Legend aren\u2019t a reasonable fix for what I take to be the existing issues with the core book system. specifically, Momentum still can\u2019t be collected at any reasonable rate unless one succeeds at a positioning roll. If a Solar has a full excellency and Salty Dog Method it\u2019s difficult to imagine anything less than four dragonblooded sailors with four ships and crack crews ever even slowing him down (the 2 die penalty for each ship beyond the first would be decisive in that circumstance).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile giving the winner of the contest momentum equal to the total of their successes (in Crucible of Legend) rather than just net successes (from the core book) exacerbates the issue of a winner take all system. Of the five ships in the core book, only one has a positive maneuverability and two have maneuverability penalties. So the change of giving a losing character momentum equal to their ship\u2019s maneuverability minimum 1, means giving the loser just 1 eighty percent of the time, which is pretty meaningless.<br /> <br /> My first thought is to award momentum for a positioning maneuver equal to 4 + ship\u2019s maneuverability bonus + net successes (if any). That puts the timing for doing things other than positioning actions at one every 3 turns even if you can\u2019t win an opposed roll.<br /> <br /> The 2 momentum discount for the first time in a scene a ship tries a specific maneuver doesn\u2019t make sense from a descriptive point of view and it doesn\u2019t actually solve the issue of ships having too little momentum. I think it does more harm than good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}